      "id": "claim_937b0d08bd3849b4b3ddd56a5664ca43",
      "statement": "The Go server entrypoint constructs three independent ZeroHub instances (static, random, and IP hub modes) via a shared newZeroHubOrPanic constructor and passes them to the handler, so each hub mode is backed by its own hub registry; the former 'permanent' mode was merged into the never-expiring static mode.",
